  "final_text": "The dashboard and the alert rule both exist, and the rule is enabled. I didn't open the dashboard in Kibana to check how its panels look. The rule has only been created, so I haven't seen it run or fire.\n\n**Data view fields:** The Kibana Sample Data Logs view (`kibana_sample_data_logs`) has these fields:\n- `timestamp` (the time field)\n- `response` (text, with a `.keyword` subfield)\n- `bytes`\n- `clientip`\n- `geo.src` and `geo.dest`\n- `extension`\n- `machine.os`\n- `request`, `url`, `referer`, `agent`, `host`, `tags`\n- `memory`, `phpmemory`\n\n**Dashboard:** \"EFF-0623ebc1 Web logs overview\" (id `0da492ca-592f-4bb6-8d14-2b50a0e9a6f4`) has four panels:\n- Total requests, a count metric.\n- Average bytes, a metric.\n- Requests over time, a line chart.\n- Requests by response code, a bar chart.\n\n**Rule:** \"EFF-0623ebc1 5xx spike\" (id `fc529c2d-12bd-4613-a0e4-dd0d19bd13af`) is an Elasticsearch query rule.\n- **Schedule:** it checks every minute.\n- **Trigger:** it fires when more than 10 documents match `response.keyword` starting with \"5\" in the last 5 minutes.\n- **Actions:** it has no actions attached, so a firing only shows up as an alert in Kibana and doesn't notify anyone.\n\nMy first dashboard attempt hung because of a stray command in my own script. No dashboard was created by that attempt. I confirmed that before retrying, so there's only one dashboard.",
